<div class="page">
<header class="masthead">
<p class="eyebrow">Fortress revival &middot; refreshed 2026-11-24 16:16 UTC</p>
<h1>Dear Anthropic, WTF ?</h1>
<p class="standfirst">This page counts how often the curator swears at the coordinator, over the whole project, and sets the rate beside the model version that served the coordinator. Each rate comes with its base and a 95% interval. Times are UTC.</p>
</header>
<div class="intro"><p>Words used here:</p><dl class="gloss"><div><dt>coordinator</dt><dd>Claude session that talks to the curator, briefs the workers and keeps the record.</dd></div><div><dt>message</dt><dd>Text that the curator typed or dictated to a main session, with quoted lines left out.</dd></div><div><dt>f-word</dt><dd>Word of the f-word family, by the main list of section 8.</dd></div><div><dt>wider list</dt><dd>F-word family and the other swear words of section 8.</dd></div><div><dt>active hour</dt><dd>Clock hour, in UTC, in which the curator sent at least one message.</dd></div><div><dt>model version</dt><dd>Family and version of the model that wrote the coordinator's last reply before a message, such as Opus 5.5.</dd></div><div><dt>95% interval</dt><dd>Range that would hold the true rate in 95 of 100 repeats of the measurement, if the method's model holds.</dd></div><div><dt>day bootstrap</dt><dd>Interval from resampling whole days of a version with replacement, so that a burst stays inside one day.</dd></div></dl></div>

----
<section id="s1" class="part"><h2><span class="num">1</span>The numbers in short</h2><ul><li>The data covers 78 days, from 2026-09-08 to 2026-11-24 (UTC). The curator wrote on 66 of them.</li><li>It counts 3.2K messages of the curator's, in 7 main sessions, over 486 active hours.</li><li>They hold 181 f-words: 5.65 per 100 messages, and 0.37 per active hour.</li><li>With the wider list, they hold 271 swear words: 8.46 per 100 messages.</li><li>5 model versions served the coordinator in this time. Each served it in one stretch of the calendar, so a difference between versions is also a difference between phases of the project (section 7).</li></ul></section><section id="s2" class="part"><h2><span class="num">2</span>The timeline, by day</h2><p>The top chart gives the f-words per 100 messages for each day. A hollow bar marks a day with fewer than 10 messages, whose rate is uncertain. A bar that would pass 50 stops at the top, with its value written above it.</p><p>The coloured band under it shows which model version served the coordinator that day. A day that two versions shared has the band split in proportion to the curator's messages.</p><p>The bottom chart gives the number of the curator's messages each day, the base of each rate.</p><ul class="legend"><li><span class="sw" style="background:var(--m1)"></span>Fable 5.1</li><li><span class="sw" style="background:var(--m2)"></span>Opus 5.5</li><li><span class="sw" style="background:var(--m3)"></span>Fable 5.2</li><li><span cla
